quiz({
  q: "In the recipe, which change raises KR-20 while leaving the true reliability where it was?",
  options: [
    {text: "Scale the true-score and error variances up by the same factor", correct: true, why: "Reliability, $\\sigma^2_T/(\\sigma^2_T + \\sigma^2_E)$, is unchanged, but the variance of the total grows while the item variances don't, so KR-20 rises."},
    {text: "Add respondents", correct: false, why: "More respondents make both numbers more precise. They don't move either one systematically."},
    {text: "Nothing: KR-20 is tied to reliability", correct: false, why: "Only through assumptions about the items. Here the items' errors are correlated, so KR-20 follows the variance of the total instead."}
